# Runtime data. Nothing in this directory is tracked except this file.
#
# Everything here is written by a running controller: per-machine, usually
# per-boot, and some of it is secret — `auth/bootstrap.token`, the TLS keys in
# `certs/`, and whole input payloads in `dlq/`. None of it is a fixture, and
# every directory is recreated on demand (`File.mkdir_p!`), so losing the lot
# costs nothing but a restart. `docs/topics/core/running_and_testing.md` covers wiping it.
#
# Deny by default, on purpose. The previous rule listed the subdirectories one
# by one, which meant a subsystem that started writing here was tracked until
# somebody noticed — `dlq/` sat untracked in `git status` for exactly that
# reason, and it holds parked payloads. A new subsystem is now covered the day
# it appears.
#
# If something here ever does need tracking, add an explicit `!` line for that
# path and say why — but prefer somewhere outside the runtime data directory.
*
!.gitignore
